# THE PARTS THAT CROSS A DOCUMENT, WHICH IS THE `callActivity` POPULATION AND NO LONGER THE WHOLE
# PART TABLE. One row per part whose target lives in another filing.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE PIN IS IN THE FILE NAME BECAUSE IT IS NOT IN THE KEY, AND A RELATION THAT RESTRICTS A DIMENSION MUST DECLARE IT. `calls`
#    used to expect `|callActivity| + |subProcess| = |part|`, one law over two elements, and that
#    is what let a LOCAL part be rendered as a flow node at all. A local fusion is a partition of
#    the composed layer, not an activity inside it, so the two halves are now two laws.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND SPLITTING THEM IS WHAT LETS THE `invents` STATE BE MEASURED. Only a foreign part goes
#   through `calledElement`, which is a QName of a PROCESS, and that is the flattening that can put
#   a cycle in the emitted call graph which `F` does not have. A law over the union of both could
#   not say how much of the emission was exposed to it. This one can: it IS the exposed population.
-- diagrams/calls.sqlc pinned to the parts that leave their own document.
SELECT c.composition, c.composed_layer, c.part_notation, c.part_filing, c.part_layer
FROM (
    :compose(diagrams/calls.sqlc)
) c
WHERE NOT c.is_local
